I now have the complete call chain. Here is the full picture of everything that happens on `POST /api/owners`.

## Summary of the call chain

`POST /api/owners` → `OwnersApi.addOwner` (generated, does `@Valid` bean validation) → `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (maps DTO→entity, duplicate checks, sets customer code) → `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner` → `OwnerRepository.save` (JPA `persist`) → JPA `@PrePersist` on `Owner` defaults the registration date. Entity setters (`setTelephone`, `setEmail`) normalize values. Errors surface through `ExceptionControllerAdvice`.

There are **no** custom validators, no validation groups, no published events, no `@EventListener` handlers, no email/notification sending, and no relevant filters/interceptors. The only side-effects beyond persistence are logging in the exception advice and the JPA lifecycle callback.

---

## 1. The controller method (POST /api/owners)

The route is declared on the generated interface and implemented by the V1 controller.

**Generated mapping** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/api/OwnersApi.java`

- Line 44: `@Validated` on the interface (enables method-parameter Bean Validation).
- Lines 52, 79–87: the mapping and the `@Valid @RequestBody` binding:
```java
String PATH_ADD_OWNER = "/owners";
@RequestMapping(
    method = RequestMethod.POST,
    value = OwnersApi.PATH_ADD_OWNER,
    produces = { "application/json" },
    consumes = { "application/json" }
)
default ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(
    @Parameter(name = "OwnerFieldsDto", description = "The pet owner", required = true) @Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto
) { ... }
```
The base path `/api` comes from `@RequestMapping("/api")` on the controller, so the full path is `/api/owners`.

**Actual implementation** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`, lines 100–117:
```java
@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
@Override
public ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
    HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
    Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto);
    Collection<Owner> owners = this.clinicService.findAllOwners();
    boolean sharesHousehold = Boolean.TRUE.equals(ownerFieldsDto.getSharesHousehold());
    if (owners.stream().anyMatch(existing -> existing.getTelephone().equals(owner.getTelephone()))
            || (!sharesHousehold && owners.stream().anyMatch(existing -> sameHousehold(existing, owner)))) {
        return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);
    }
    owner.setCustomerCode(CustomerCode.of(owner.getLastName(), owners.size()));
    this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);
    OwnerDto ownerDto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
    headers.setLocation(UriComponentsBuilder.newInstance()
        .path("/api/owners/{id}").buildAndExpand(owner.getId()).toUri());
    return new ResponseEntity<>(ownerDto, headers, HttpStatus.CREATED);
}
```

**Order of operations inside the controller:**
1. Authorization: `@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")` (before the method runs).
2. Map DTO → `Owner` entity via `ownerMapper.toOwner(...)` (this triggers entity setters — see normalization in section 8).
3. Load **all** owners: `clinicService.findAllOwners()`.
4. Duplicate-telephone check: rejects with **409 CONFLICT** if any existing owner has the same (normalized) telephone.
5. Duplicate-household check: unless `sharesHousehold == true`, rejects with **409 CONFLICT** if any existing owner has the same last name + normalized address (`sameHousehold`, lines 121–125).
6. Sets `customerCode` via `CustomerCode.of(lastName, owners.size())`.
7. Persists via `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`.
8. Builds `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header and returns **201 CREATED** with the `OwnerDto`.

The household comparison helper (lines 119–125):
```java
private static boolean sameHousehold(Owner a, Owner b) {
    return a.getLastName().equalsIgnoreCase(b.getLastName())
        && a.getAddress().trim().replaceAll("\\s+", " ")
            .equalsIgnoreCase(b.getAddress().trim().replaceAll("\\s+", " "));
}
```

Note: a second controller exists (`OwnerRestControllerV2` at `.../controller/v2/OwnerRestControllerV2.java`) but it only implements a paged **GET** list; it does not handle owner creation.

---

## 2. Request DTO used as `@RequestBody` and all Bean Validation annotations

`@RequestBody` type is `OwnerFieldsDto` — `/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/dto/OwnerFieldsDto.java` (generated from the OpenAPI spec). Constraints are on the getters:

- **firstName** (line 71): `@NotNull @Pattern(regexp = "^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$") @Size(min = 1, max = 30)`
- **lastName** (line 92): `@NotNull @Pattern(regexp = "^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$") @Size(min = 1, max = 30)`
- **address** (line 113): `@NotNull @Pattern(regexp = "^.*\\S.*$") @Size(min = 1, max = 255)`
- **city** (line 134): `@NotNull @Pattern(regexp = "^.*\\S.*$") @Size(min = 1, max = 80)`
- **telephone** (line 155): `@NotNull @Pattern(regexp = "^[ \\-()]*(\\+[ \\-()]*(\\d[ \\-()]*){8,15}|0[ \\-()]*(\\d[ \\-()]*){6,13}|[1-9][ \\-()]*(\\d[ \\-()]*){5,12})$") @Size(min = 1, max = 20)`
- **email** (line 176): `@Size(max = 255) @jakarta.validation.constraints.Email` (optional / nullable)
