**Normalization performed by entity setters** (invoked during MapStruct mapping `ownerMapper.toOwner`):
- `setTelephone` (lines 115–117): `telephone = PhoneNumbers.toE164(telephone)` — strips spaces/dashes/brackets; keeps `+` and country code, otherwise assumes `+61` and drops a single leading `0`. See `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/PhoneNumbers.java` (lines 34–43). This is why the duplicate-telephone check in the controller compares normalized values.
